{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QmmFxmoT4GDxHqemhawn9o","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"The Edwards–McDermid degree-sequence bound on pathwidth, evaluated (loop0012\nitem 01; `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §1; the plan is\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md`).\n\nEdwards & McDermid, *Algorithmica* 72(4):940–968, 2015, Corollary 5.2:\n\n    pw(G) ≤ Σ_{v ∈ V(r(G))} g_{1/6}(d_{r(G)}(v)) + τ(|V(G)|) + O(log |V(G)|),\n\nwhere `g = g_{1/6}` is the weight function of their Section 3.1 (`g(2) = 0`,\n`g(3) = 1/6`, `n g(n) = (n − 2) g(n − 1) + g(n − 2) + 1` for `n ≥ 4`), `r(G)`\nis the series-parallel reduction of `G` (their Section 3.2: delete vertices of\ndegree ≤ 1, suppress vertices of degree 2, until every degree is ≥ 3 or the\ngraph is empty), and `τ(n) = o(n)` is the error term of Fomin & Høie's cubic\nbound, for which the paper gives no constant.\n\nEverything here is exact: `g` in `fractions.Fraction`, graphs as adjacency bit\nmasks (`adj[v]` has bit `u` iff `u ~ v`), the reduction with a bucket of\nlow-degree vertices so that it is linear in the number of steps (the dataset\nhas graphs to 2,916 vertices). Removed vertices are *isolated*, as in the Lean\ndesign (plan §0.5): `reduce` returns the reduced adjacency on the same vertex\nset and the mask of removed vertices, and `g(0) = g(1) = g(2) = 0` makes them\nweightless.\n\nNothing here solves a pathwidth; the pathwidths come from the record.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport math\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nfrom typing import Iterable\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"g\", \"g_float\", \"g_real\", \"g_prime\", \"alternating_factorial\", \"g_closed_form\",\n    \"popcount\", \"bits\", \"from_edges\", \"from_networkx\", \"degrees\", \"edge_count\",\n    \"components\", \"min_degree\", \"reduce\", \"main_term\", \"histogram_term\",\n    \"average_degree\", \"average_degree_term\", \"fminus\", \"f_potential\",\n    \"is_reduced\", \"is_cubic\", \"poisson_value\", \"fomin_hoie_n_eps\", \"fomin_hoie_budget\",\n    \"evaluate\",\n    # item 02: the reduction system step by step, basic graphs, the paper's\n    # choice of `w`, Algorithm X, the one-component potential\n    \"support\", \"isolate\", \"isolate_set\", \"restrict\", \"step_vertices\", \"sp_step\",\n    \"reduce_random\", \"global_min_degree\", \"F_global\", \"is_basic_component\", \"is_basic\",\n    \"paper_choice\", \"algorithm_x\", \"pathwidth_induced\",\n]\n\nALPHA = Fraction(1, 6)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the weights\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\ndef g(n: int) -> Fraction:\n    \"\"\"`g_{1/6}(n)` in exact rationals; `g(0) = g(1) = g(2) = 0`, `g(3) = 1/6`,\n    and `n g(n) = (n − 2) g(n − 1) + g(n − 2) + 1` for `n ≥ 4` (paper p. 6).\"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"g is defined on the naturals\")\n    if n <= 2:\n        return Fraction(0)\n    if n == 3:\n        return ALPHA\n    return ((n - 2) * g(n - 1) + g(n - 2) + 1) / n\n\n\ndef g_float(n: int) -> float:\n    return float(g(n))\n\n\ndef g_real(x: float | Fraction) -> Fraction:\n    \"\"\"The paper's linear interpolation between integers (p. 6), exact when `x`\n    is a `Fraction`; below 2 it is 0, since `g(0) = g(1) = g(2) = 0`.\"\"\"\n    x = Fraction(x)\n    if x < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"g_real is defined on x ≥ 0\")\n    n = math.floor(x)\n    t = x - n\n    return (1 - t) * g(n) + t * g(n + 1)\n56:def g(n: int) -> Fraction:\n68:def g_float(n: int) -> float:\n72:def g_real(x: float | Fraction) -> Fraction:\n83:def g_prime(n: int) -> Fraction:\n90:def alternating_factorial(n: int) -> int:\n100:def g_closed_form(n: int, alpha: Fraction = ALPHA) -> Fraction:\n114:def popcount(x: int) -> int:\n118:def bits(mask: int) -> Iterable[int]:\n126:def from_edges(n: int, edges: Iterable[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[int]:\n136:def from_networkx(G) -> list[int]:\n143:def degrees(adj: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n147:def edge_count(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n151:def components(adj: list[int], support_only: bool = True) -> list[int]:\n176:def min_degree(adj: list[int], mask: int) -> int:\n180:def is_reduced(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n185:def is_cubic(adj: list[int], mask: int | None = None) -> bool:\n195:def reduce(adj: list[int]) -> tuple[list[int], int]:\n266:def histogram_term(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n272:def main_term(adj: list[int], reduced: tuple[list[int], int] | None = None) -> Fraction:\n279:def average_degree(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n286:def average_degree_term(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n292:def f_potential(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n297:def fminus(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n313:def poisson_value(c: float, tail: float = 1e-15) -> float:\n333:def fomin_hoie_n_eps(eps: float) -> float:\n338:def fomin_hoie_budget(n: int) -> float:\n363:def evaluate(adj: list[int], pw: int | None = None) -> dict:\n407:def support(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n416:def isolate(adj: list[int], w: int) -> list[int]:\n425:def isolate_set(adj: list[int], X: int) -> list[int]:\n432:def restrict(adj: list[int], C: int) -> list[int]:\n437:def step_vertices(adj: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n444:def sp_step(adj: list[int], v: int) -> list[int]:\n464:def reduce_random(adj: list[int], rng) -> list[int]:\n476:def global_min_degree(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n482:def F_global(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n490:def is_basic_component(adj: list[int], C: int) -> bool:\n503:def is_basic(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n508:def paper_choice(adj: list[int], C: int | None = None) -> tuple[list[int], list[int], int]:\n523:def algorithm_x(adj: list[int], rng=None) -> tuple[int, list[int]]:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e40014c-07da-4ca6-b155-734093dbcc62","uuid":"1830c5a0-dd7e-4825-afda-abcdd28bde82","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:35:28.586Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"The Edwards–McDermid degree-sequence bound on pathwidth, evaluated (loop0012\nitem 01; `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §1; the plan is\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md`).\n\nEdwards & McDermid, *Algorithmica* 72(4):940–968, 2015, Corollary 5.2:\n\n    pw(G) ≤ Σ_{v ∈ V(r(G))} g_{1/6}(d_{r(G)}(v)) + τ(|V(G)|) + O(log |V(G)|),\n\nwhere `g = g_{1/6}` is the weight function of their Section 3.1 (`g(2) = 0`,\n`g(3) = 1/6`, `n g(n) = (n − 2) g(n − 1) + g(n − 2) + 1` for `n ≥ 4`), `r(G)`\nis the series-parallel reduction of `G` (their Section 3.2: delete vertices of\ndegree ≤ 1, suppress vertices of degree 2, until every degree is ≥ 3 or the\ngraph is empty), and `τ(n) = o(n)` is the error term of Fomin & Høie's cubic\nbound, for which the paper gives no constant.\n\nEverything here is exact: `g` in `fractions.Fraction`, graphs as adjacency bit\nmasks (`adj[v]` has bit `u` iff `u ~ v`), the reduction with a bucket of\nlow-degree vertices so that it is linear in the number of steps (the dataset\nhas graphs to 2,916 vertices). Removed vertices are *isolated*, as in the Lean\ndesign (plan §0.5): `reduce` returns the reduced adjacency on the same vertex\nset and the mask of removed vertices, and `g(0) = g(1) = g(2) = 0` makes them\nweightless.\n\nNothing here solves a pathwidth; the pathwidths come from the record.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport math\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nfrom typing import Iterable\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"g\", \"g_float\", \"g_real\", \"g_prime\", \"alternating_factorial\", \"g_closed_form\",\n    \"popcount\", \"bits\", \"from_edges\", \"from_networkx\", \"degrees\", \"edge_count\",\n    \"components\", \"min_degree\", \"reduce\", \"main_term\", \"histogram_term\",\n    \"average_degree\", \"average_degree_term\", \"fminus\", \"f_potential\",\n    \"is_reduced\", \"is_cubic\", \"poisson_value\", \"fomin_hoie_n_eps\", \"fomin_hoie_budget\",\n    \"evaluate\",\n    # item 02: the reduction system step by step, basic graphs, the paper's\n    # choice of `w`, Algorithm X, the one-component potential\n    \"support\", \"isolate\", \"isolate_set\", \"restrict\", \"step_vertices\", \"sp_step\",\n    \"reduce_random\", \"global_min_degree\", \"F_global\", \"is_basic_component\", \"is_basic\",\n    \"paper_choice\", \"algorithm_x\", \"pathwidth_induced\",\n]\n\nALPHA = Fraction(1, 6)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the weights\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\ndef g(n: int) -> Fraction:\n    \"\"\"`g_{1/6}(n)` in exact rationals; `g(0) = g(1) = g(2) = 0`, `g(3) = 1/6`,\n    and `n g(n) = (n − 2) g(n − 1) + g(n − 2) + 1` for `n ≥ 4` (paper p. 6).\"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"g is defined on the naturals\")\n    if n <= 2:\n        return Fraction(0)\n    if n == 3:\n        return ALPHA\n    return ((n - 2) * g(n - 1) + g(n - 2) + 1) / n\n\n\ndef g_float(n: int) -> float:\n    return float(g(n))\n\n\ndef g_real(x: float | Fraction) -> Fraction:\n    \"\"\"The paper's linear interpolation between integers (p. 6), exact when `x`\n    is a `Fraction`; below 2 it is 0, since `g(0) = g(1) = g(2) = 0`.\"\"\"\n    x = Fraction(x)\n    if x < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"g_real is defined on x ≥ 0\")\n    n = math.floor(x)\n    t = x - n\n    return (1 - t) * g(n) + t * g(n + 1)\n56:def g(n: int) -> Fraction:\n68:def g_float(n: int) -> float:\n72:def g_real(x: float | Fraction) -> Fraction:\n83:def g_prime(n: int) -> Fraction:\n90:def alternating_factorial(n: int) -> int:\n100:def g_closed_form(n: int, alpha: Fraction = ALPHA) -> Fraction:\n114:def popcount(x: int) -> int:\n118:def bits(mask: int) -> Iterable[int]:\n126:def from_edges(n: int, edges: Iterable[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[int]:\n136:def from_networkx(G) -> list[int]:\n143:def degrees(adj: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n147:def edge_count(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n151:def components(adj: list[int], support_only: bool = True) -> list[int]:\n176:def min_degree(adj: list[int], mask: int) -> int:\n180:def is_reduced(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n185:def is_cubic(adj: list[int], mask: int | None = None) -> bool:\n195:def reduce(adj: list[int]) -> tuple[list[int], int]:\n266:def histogram_term(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n272:def main_term(adj: list[int], reduced: tuple[list[int], int] | None = None) -> Fraction:\n279:def average_degree(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n286:def average_degree_term(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n292:def f_potential(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n297:def fminus(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n313:def poisson_value(c: float, tail: float = 1e-15) -> float:\n333:def fomin_hoie_n_eps(eps: float) -> float:\n338:def fomin_hoie_budget(n: int) -> float:\n363:def evaluate(adj: list[int], pw: int | None = None) -> dict:\n407:def support(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n416:def isolate(adj: list[int], w: int) -> list[int]:\n425:def isolate_set(adj: list[int], X: int) -> list[int]:\n432:def restrict(adj: list[int], C: int) -> list[int]:\n437:def step_vertices(adj: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n444:def sp_step(adj: list[int], v: int) -> list[int]:\n464:def reduce_random(adj: list[int], rng) -> list[int]:\n476:def global_min_degree(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n482:def F_global(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n490:def is_basic_component(adj: list[int], C: int) -> bool:\n503:def is_basic(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n508:def paper_choice(adj: list[int], C: int | None = None) -> tuple[list[int], list[int], int]:\n523:def algorithm_x(adj: list[int], rng=None) -> tuple[int, list[int]]:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QmmFxmoT4GDxHqemhawn9o","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
