{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0183oLAmrPm2GW7gNrQJjnFw","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Axiom audit of every theorem the draft cites (loop0008 item 09).\n\n    python -m paper1.latex.check_axioms            # coverage, then run Lean\n    python -m paper1.latex.check_axioms --no-lean  # coverage only (no build)\n\nTwo checks.\n\n1. **Coverage.** Every theorem or lemma named in a `\\\\lean{...}` footnote or a\n   `\\\\path{...}` cell of `sec*.tex` has a `#print axioms` line in\n   `paper1/axiom_check.lean`. Definitions (`def`, `structure`, ...) are\n   skipped: they carry no proof.\n2. **Axioms.** `lake env lean ../paper1/axiom_check.lean` is run from `lean/`,\n   and every line must report exactly `propext`, `Classical.choice` and\n   `Quot.sound` (until 2026-10-31 `conjecture_sqrt_tw_f6` was a control\n   expected to show `sorryAx`; it is proved now). Needs a built `lean/`\n   (`lake build`), takes a few seconds.\n\nExits non-zero on any failure.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom paper1.latex.check_lean import LEAN, cited\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nAXIOM_CHECK = ROOT / \"paper1\" / \"axiom_check.lean\"\nEXPECTED = {\"propext\", \"Classical.choice\", \"Quot.sound\"}\nTHEOREM = re.compile(r\"^\\s*(?:@\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\s*)?(?:private\\s+|protected\\s+)*\"\n                     r\"(?:theorem|lemma)\\s+([^\\s:({\\[]+)\", re.M)\n\n\ndef theorem_names() -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"Last components of every theorem or lemma under lean/MOSPFormalization/.\"\"\"\n    names: set[str] = set()\n    for p in LEAN.rglob(\"*.lean\"):\n        names.update(m.group(1).split(\".\")[-1] for m in THEOREM.finditer(p.read_text()))\n    return names\n\n\ndef printed() -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"Last components of the names `axiom_check.lean` prints.\"\"\"\n    return {line.split()[-1].split(\".\")[-1]\n            for line in AXIOM_CHECK.read_text().splitlines()\n            if line.startswith(\"#print axioms\")}\n\n\ndef uncovered() -> list[str]:\n    theorems, have = theorem_names(), printed()\n    return sorted(n for n in cited()\n                  if n.split(\".\")[-1] in theorems and n.split(\".\")[-1] not in have)\n\n\ndef run_lean() -> tuple[int, list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Run the axiom check; return (lines checked, failures).\"\"\"\n    out = subprocess.run([\"lake\", \"env\", \"lean\", str(AXIOM_CHECK)], cwd=ROOT / \"lean\",\n01_verify\n02_lemmas\nSHA256\nem2015.pdf\nem2015.txt\n11:  W1–W5  recurrence, g non-decreasing, g' non-increasing from 3, property 6,\n427:# W1–W5 (main process)\n434:        assert d * g(d) == (d - 2) * g(d - 1) + g(d - 2) + 1, d          # W1\n436:        assert g(d + 1) >= g(d), d                                       # W2 (Lemma 8.3)\n438:        assert g_prime(d + 1) <= g_prime(d), d                           # W3 (Lemma 8.4)\n440:        assert 1 - g(d) == (d - 1) * g_prime(d) + g_prime(d - 1), d      # W4 (property 6)\n442:        assert 0 <= g(d) < 1, d                                          # W5a\n443:        assert 0 <= g_prime(d) <= Fraction(1, 6), d                      # W5b\n445:        assert g_closed_form(d) == g(d), d                               # W5c (Lemma 8.1)\n454:    out.append(f\"W1–W5 hold to n = {N} in exact rationals: recurrence (W1), g non-decreasing (W2), \"\n455:               f\"g' non-increasing from 3 (W3), property 6 (W4), 0 ≤ g < 1 and 0 ≤ g' ≤ 1/6 (W5), \"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e40014c-07da-4ca6-b155-734093dbcc62","uuid":"49e98740-2370-4a38-9c88-35ae366ede90","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:37:38.657Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Axiom audit of every theorem the draft cites (loop0008 item 09).\n\n    python -m paper1.latex.check_axioms            # coverage, then run Lean\n    python -m paper1.latex.check_axioms --no-lean  # coverage only (no build)\n\nTwo checks.\n\n1. **Coverage.** Every theorem o